{% endfor %}
Use "verified" only for claims directly supported by cited source text.
Anything you reasoned to rather than read is not verified.
{% endif %}

confidence must be one of: high, moderate, low, none.
  high      — multiple independent tier1/tier2 sources agree, no live contradictions
  moderate  — decent support, some gaps or single-source load-bearing claims
  low       — thin sourcing, heavy inference, or unresolved conflicts
  none      — the sources do not answer this

Reply with ONLY this JSON object:
{
  "answer": "direct prose answer to the question, 1-4 paragraphs. Cite source IDs inline like [S3] or [S1,S7].",
  "confidence": "high|moderate|low|none",
  "key_findings": [
    {"claim": "...", "tag": "verified", "sources": ["S1","S4"]}
  ],
  "contradictions": [
    {"claim": "source A says X, source B says Y", "tag": "verified", "sources": ["S2","S9"]}
  ],
  "gaps": [
    "what this research did not establish and why"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "anything about source quality, recency, or bias the reader must know"
  ]
}
